== For the noodles ==

Cook the @rice noodles{8%ounces} in a well-salted #pot of boiling water until al dente. Drain and toss with a small amount of @cooking oil{1%teaspoon} to keep the noodles from sticking together.

In a small #saucepot, whisk together the @sriracha{3%tablespoons}, @honey{2%tablespoons}, @rice vinegar{2%tablespoons}, @soy sauce{1%tablespoon}, @lime juice{1%tablespoon}, and @vegetable broth{1/4%cup}. Taste for seasonings and adjust as needed. For more spice, add 1 tablespoon sriracha at a time. For more sweetness, add 1-2 teaspoons honey at a time.

Bring to a simmer over medium-high heat. In a small #container, whisk together @corn starch{1%teaspoon} and @water{1%teaspoon} to form a cornstarch slurry. Add this to the sauce and reduce heat to a gentle simmer over low heat.

Simmer, whisking occasionally, until thickened. This will take just ~{2-3%minutes}. For a thicker sauce, repeat the corn starch slurry. For a thinner sauce, add an extra splash of vegetable broth.

Toss the noodles with the sauce. Serve with steamed broccoli and air fryer tofu for a complete meal.

== For the complete meal ==

Steam @broccoli{1-2%crowns} until vivid green and tender. I use a #steamer basket{} over 1 inch of simmering water, but a #fine mesh sieve{} with a #lid fitted on top also works. Season with @kosher salt{1/4%teaspoon} and @black pepper{1/2%teaspoon}, to taste.

Press the @extra-firm tofu{14%ounce block} for ~{5%minutes} with a #tofu press{} or by wrapping it in #paper towels{} and weighing it down with something heavy, like a #cast iron skillet{}.

Tear the tofu into bite-sized pieces. In a #mixing bowl{}, whisk together @canola oil{1%teaspoon}, @nutritional yeast{1%tablespoon}, black pepper, and salt (can adjust to taste as needed.) Toss the tofu in the seasonings and add more oil as needed to fully coat the tofu.

Transfer the tofu to the #air fryer rack{}. Air fry at 375F for ~{15-20%minutes}, or until crisp and golden. Serve the broccoli and tofu with the noodles.